From 9520f059f347315224010a206f3b4b4038baf959 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang YiHe <108562510+nmhjklnm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:26:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Preserve streamed text on a repeated start of the same
 message

Why: Claude Code 2.1.304 with a gateway can emit another message_start for
an already-streamed API message before its consolidated assistant message.
Clearing the delivered prefix at that point repeats every answer in Gugu.
Reset only for a different or missing API message id, independently for
each parent stream. Retain the existing fallback for id-less gateways.

Upstream: none yet; reproduced in the source-level regression test from a
real SDK event sequence during Gugu issue #7582 acceptance.
Drop: when upstream preserves the delivered prefix across repeated starts
of the same API message and includes equivalent regression coverage.
---
 src/acp-agent.ts            | 12 ++++++++++--
 src/tests/acp-agent.test.ts | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/acp-agent.ts b/src/acp-agent.ts
index 7efe84c..e0fd9da 100644
--- a/src/acp-agent.ts
+++ b/src/acp-agent.ts
@@ -4483,6 +4483,7 @@ export class ClaudeAcpAgent {
